If there is a clinician then it is recommended that the clinician does not consider a first-line-opioid-therapy for a subacute-pain.
If there is a clinician then it is recommended that the clinician does not consider a routine-opioid-therapy for a subacute-pain.
If there is a clinician then it is recommended that the clinician does not consider a first-line-opioid-therapy for a chronic-pain.
If there is a clinician then it is recommended that the clinician does not consider a routine-opioid-therapy for a chronic-pain.
If a patient has a subacute-pain and there is an opioid-therapy then it is recommended that the opioid-therapy is not first-line for the subacute-pain.
If a patient has a chronic-pain and there is an opioid-therapy then it is recommended that the opioid-therapy is not first-line for the chronic-pain.
